{
  "name": "Prostate Cancer Module",
  "gmf_version": 2,
  "remarks": [
    "Prostate cancer screening, diagnosis, treatment and progression for men 55+.",
    "",
    "ENCOUNTER DISCIPLINE: ModSynthea gives each person a single encounter",
    "reservation (State.java Encounter/EncounterEnd). Every Encounter opened here",
    "reaches an EncounterEnd before any Delay or Guard, and every Delay sits",
    "between an EncounterEnd and the next Encounter. The only Delay inside an open",
    "encounter is Prostatectomy_Stay, which is a genuine inpatient length of stay.",
    "",
    "CALIBRATION TARGETS (see per-state remarks for the arithmetic):",
    "- Lifetime probability of a prostate cancer diagnosis ~12.7% (SEER 2018-2022:",
    "  lifetime risk 1 in 8, ~12.9%; median age at diagnosis 67).",
    "- Screening offered ages 55-69 only (USPSTF 2018, JAMA 319:1901 - shared",
    "  decision making 55-69, no routine PSA screening at 70+), with 40% annual",
    "  participation (Fedewa, JAMA Intern Med 2017), so a man averages ~6",
    "  screening visits across the window rather than 15.",
    "- Biochemical recurrence after definitive treatment ~30% by 10 years",
    "  (Han, J Urol 2003; Freedland, JAMA 2005), then discharge to survivorship.",
    "- Castration resistance ~9%/yr on ADT, with explicit stable-on-ADT exit",
    "  (blend of SWOG 9346 metastatic hormone-sensitive and Kirby, Int J Clin",
    "  Pract 2011 M0 biochemical recurrence).",
    "- Prostate cancer death arises only in the metastatic castration-resistant",
    "  arm, at 25%/yr (median mCRPC survival ~2.4 yr; TAX327, NEJM 2004). Chained",
    "  through the graph this puts cause-specific mortality at ~13-16% of",
    "  diagnosed men, against a real ~19% (SEER: 2.5% lifetime prostate cancer",
    "  mortality over 12.9% lifetime incidence).",
    "",
    "ATTRIBUTES (all module-local except 'Prostate Cancer', which",
    "home_hospice_snf.json and veteran_prostate_cancer.json also read):",
    "  Prostate Cancer         - the ConditionOnset entry, set at diagnosis",
    "  last_observation        - most recent PSA value in ng/mL (a real number:",
    "                            Observation states cannot assign_to_attribute, so",
    "                            each PSA value is drawn by a SetAttribute and then",
    "                            read back by the Observation via 'attribute')",
    "  prostate_cancer_risk    - NCCN risk group at diagnosis",
    "  clinical_stage          - clinical T stage at diagnosis",
    "  prostate_followup_years - completed post-treatment surveillance years"
  ],
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "Male_Check"
    },
    "Male_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Gender",
            "gender": "M"
          },
          "transition": "Screening_Age_Guard"
        },
        {
          "transition": "Terminal"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Screening_Age_Guard": {
      "type": "Guard",
      "remarks": [
        "USPSTF 2018 (JAMA 319:1901) recommends individualised PSA screening for",
        "men aged 55-69. Nobody enters the screening loop before 55."
      ],
      "allow": {
        "condition_type": "Age",
        "operator": ">=",
        "quantity": 55,
        "unit": "years"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Screening_Entry_Delay"
    },
    "Screening_Entry_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "remarks": [
        "Spread first screening visits across the year following the 55th birthday",
        "so onsets are not stacked on a single anniversary date."
      ],
      "range": {
        "low": 0,
        "high": 364,
        "unit": "days"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Screening_Window_Check"
    },
    "Screening_Window_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Age-out of the screening loop at 70 (USPSTF 2018: recommends against",
        "routine PSA-based screening in men 70 and older). This is the exit that",
        "the pre-2026-08 module was missing entirely."
      ],
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": ">=",
            "quantity": 70,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "Terminal"
        },
        {
          "transition": "Screening_Uptake_Decision"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Screening_Uptake_Decision": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Annual PSA screening participation, not lifetime participation: a man who",
        "defers this year is offered again next year. 40% of US men aged 55-69",
        "report a PSA test in the past year (Fedewa, JAMA Intern Med 2017;",
        "Jemal, JAMA 2015 - uptake fell from ~48% to ~35-40% after the 2012 USPSTF",
        "recommendation). The deferred branch does NOT open an encounter, which is",
        "the point: modelling every man as screened annually inflated ambulatory",
        "carrier volume ~2.5x.",
        "",
        "Effective screening interval is therefore ~2.5 years, which is why the",
        "per-screen elevated-PSA rate below is the 4-yearly-ERSPC-like 16% rather",
        "than an annually-rescreened steady state."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.4,
          "transition": "Screening_Visit"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.6,
          "transition": "PSA_Interval_Delay"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Screening_Visit": {
      "type": "Encounter",
      "encounter_class": "ambulatory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "185347001",
          "display": "Encounter for problem"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Draw"
    },
    "PSA_Draw": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "16% of screening draws land above the 3 ng/mL referral threshold. ERSPC",
        "(Schroder, NEJM 2009) saw PSA >= 3 in 10-16% of screens on a 4-yearly",
        "interval; with 40% annual uptake the effective interval here is ~2.5",
        "years, so the top of that band is the right figure.",
        "",
        "Detection arithmetic per SCREENED year: 0.16 elevated x 0.45 confirmed on",
        "repeat x 0.3125 biopsy positive = 0.0225. Multiplied by the 0.40 annual",
        "uptake in Screening_Uptake_Decision that is 0.0090 diagnoses per calendar",
        "year, unchanged. Over the 15 years from 55 to 69 that is",
        "1 - (1 - 0.009)^15 = 12.7% lifetime, matching the SEER 2018-2022 lifetime",
        "risk of ~12.9%."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.84,
          "transition": "Set_PSA_Normal"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.16,
          "transition": "Set_PSA_Elevated"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Set_PSA_Normal": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "range": {
        "low": 0.3,
        "high": 2.9,
        "decimals": 1
      },
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Test"
    },
    "Set_PSA_Elevated": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "range": {
        "low": 3.0,
        "high": 9.9,
        "decimals": 1
      },
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Test"
    },
    "PSA_Test": {
      "type": "Observation",
      "category": "laboratory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "LOINC",
          "code": "2857-1",
          "display": "Prostate specific Ag [Mass/volume] in Serum"
        }
      ],
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "unit": "ng/mL",
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Interpretation"
    },
    "PSA_Interpretation": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "last_observation",
            "operator": ">=",
            "value": 3
          },
          "transition": "Refer_For_Repeat_PSA"
        },
        {
          "transition": "End_Screening_Visit"
        }
      ]
    },
    "End_Screening_Visit": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Interval_Delay"
    },
    "PSA_Interval_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 11,
        "high": 13,
        "unit": "months"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Screening_Window_Check"
    },
    "Refer_For_Repeat_PSA": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Delay"
    },
    "Repeat_PSA_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 4,
        "high": 10,
        "unit": "weeks"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Visit"
    },
    "Repeat_PSA_Visit": {
      "type": "Encounter",
      "encounter_class": "ambulatory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "185347001",
          "display": "Encounter for problem"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Draw"
    },
    "Repeat_PSA_Draw": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "A confirmatory draw normalises in most men: transient elevation from",
        "prostatitis, instrumentation or assay variation. 55% resolve, 45% stay",
        "above 3 ng/mL and go on to imaging and biopsy."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.55,
          "transition": "Set_PSA_Resolved"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.45,
          "transition": "Set_PSA_Confirmed"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Set_PSA_Resolved": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "range": {
        "low": 0.5,
        "high": 2.9,
        "decimals": 1
      },
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Test"
    },
    "Set_PSA_Confirmed": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "range": {
        "low": 3.0,
        "high": 14.9,
        "decimals": 1
      },
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Test"
    },
    "Repeat_PSA_Test": {
      "type": "Observation",
      "category": "laboratory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "LOINC",
          "code": "2857-1",
          "display": "Prostate specific Ag [Mass/volume] in Serum"
        }
      ],
      "attribute": "last_observation",
      "unit": "ng/mL",
      "direct_transition": "Repeat_PSA_Interpretation"
    },
    "Repeat_PSA_Interpretation": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "last_observation",
            "operator": ">=",
            "value": 3
          },
          "transition": "Refer_For_Biopsy"
        },
        {
          "transition": "End_Repeat_PSA_Visit"
        }
      ]
    },
    "End_Repeat_PSA_Visit": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Interval_Delay"
    },
    "Refer_For_Biopsy": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "Biopsy_Scheduling_Delay"
    },
    "Biopsy_Scheduling_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 2,
        "high": 6,
        "unit": "weeks"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Diagnostic_Workup_Visit"
    },
    "Diagnostic_Workup_Visit": {
      "type": "Encounter",
      "encounter_class": "ambulatory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "185347001",
          "display": "Encounter for problem"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "Biopsy_Modality_Decision"
    },
    "Biopsy_Modality_Decision": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Pre-biopsy multiparametric MRI followed by MRI/ultrasound fusion targeted",
        "biopsy is now the majority pathway (NICE NG131; PRECISION, NEJM 2018);",
        "the remainder go straight to systematic needle biopsy."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.7,
          "transition": "Prostate_MRI"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.3,
          "transition": "Prostate_Biopsy"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Prostate_MRI": {
      "type": "Procedure",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "2690005",
          "display": "Magnetic resonance imaging of pelvis"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "MRI_Fusion_Biopsy"
    },
    "MRI_Fusion_Biopsy": {
      "type": "Procedure",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "447395005",
          "display": "MRI guided biopsy of prostate"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "End_Workup_Visit"
    },
    "Prostate_Biopsy": {
      "type": "Procedure",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "65575008",
          "display": "Biopsy of prostate"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "End_Workup_Visit"
    },
    "End_Workup_Visit": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "Pathology_Turnaround_Delay"
    },
    "Pathology_Turnaround_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 5,
        "high": 14,
        "unit": "days"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Pathology_Results_Visit"
    },
    "Pathology_Results_Visit": {
      "type": "Encounter",
      "encounter_class": "ambulatory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "185347001",
          "display": "Encounter for problem"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "Cancer_Diagnosis_Decision"
    },
    "Cancer_Diagnosis_Decision": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "31.25% biopsy positivity. ERSPC saw ~24-27% on systematic biopsy",
        "(Schroder, NEJM 2009); PRECISION (NEJM 2018) detected clinically",
        "significant cancer in 38% of the MRI-targeted arm, and 70% of workups",
        "here are MRI-first, so a blended ~31% is the right figure. A negative",
        "biopsy returns the man to the screening loop rather than ending his",
        "follow-up."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.3125,
          "transition": "Diagnose_Prostate_Cancer"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.6875,
          "transition": "End_Negative_Biopsy_Visit"
        }
      ]
    },
    "End_Negative_Biopsy_Visit": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "PSA_Interval_Delay"
    },
    "Diagnose_Prostate_Cancer": {
      "type": "ConditionOnset",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "399068003",
          "display": "Malignant neoplasm of prostate"
        }
      ],
      "assign_to_attribute": "Prostate Cancer",
      "direct_transition": "Risk_Stratification"
    },
    "Risk_Stratification": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "NCCN risk group at diagnosis. Approximates the SEER 2018-2022 stage mix",
        "(local ~69%, regional ~13%, distant ~8%) expressed as risk groups.",
        "",
        "This used to be a single SetAttribute carrying a {type, value_set} object,",
        "which is not valid GMF: Gson deserialises it into a LinkedTreeMap and any",
        "downstream comparison throws. It is now a router into plain-string",
        "SetAttribute states, which is what the value_set was trying to express."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.22,
          "transition": "Set_Risk_Low"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.2,
          "transition": "Set_Risk_Favorable_Intermediate"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.2,
          "transition": "Set_Risk_Unfavorable_Intermediate"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.25,
          "transition": "Set_Risk_High"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.13,
          "transition": "Set_Risk_Very_High"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Set_Risk_Low": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
      "value": "low_risk",
      "direct_transition": "Staging_Workup"
    },
    "Set_Risk_Favorable_Intermediate": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
      "value": "favorable_intermediate",
      "direct_transition": "Staging_Workup"
    },
    "Set_Risk_Unfavorable_Intermediate": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
      "value": "unfavorable_intermediate",
      "direct_transition": "Staging_Workup"
    },
    "Set_Risk_High": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
      "value": "high_risk",
      "direct_transition": "Staging_Workup"
    },
    "Set_Risk_Very_High": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
      "value": "very_high_risk",
      "direct_transition": "Staging_Workup"
    },
    "Staging_Workup": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Clinical T stage at diagnosis, weighted towards T1c because most cases",
        "are screen-detected and impalpable (SEER 2018-2022: ~69% localised).",
        "Same bad-GMF fix as Risk_Stratification: router into plain-string",
        "SetAttribute states instead of an inline value_set object."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.4,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T1c"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.18,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T2a"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.1,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T2b"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.1,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T2c"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.12,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T3a"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.06,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T3b"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.04,
          "transition": "Set_Stage_T4"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Set_Stage_T1c": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T1c",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T2a": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T2a",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T2b": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T2b",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T2c": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T2c",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T3a": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T3a",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T3b": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T3b",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Set_Stage_T4": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "clinical_stage",
      "value": "T4",
      "direct_transition": "Genomic_Testing_Decision"
    },
    "Genomic_Testing_Decision": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.4,
          "transition": "Genomic_Testing"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.6,
          "transition": "End_Diagnosis_Visit"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Genomic_Testing": {
      "type": "Observation",
      "category": "laboratory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "LOINC",
          "code": "81070-0",
          "display": "Oncotype DX prostate cancer assay"
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "low": 10,
        "high": 80,
        "decimals": 0
      },
      "unit": "{score}",
      "direct_transition": "End_Diagnosis_Visit"
    },
    "End_Diagnosis_Visit": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "direct_transition": "Treatment_Planning_Delay"
    },
    "Treatment_Planning_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "range": {
        "low": 14,
        "high": 28,
        "unit": "days"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Treatment_Discussion"
    },
    "Treatment_Discussion": {
      "type": "Encounter",
      "encounter_class": "ambulatory",
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "287051000000107",
          "display": "Multidisciplinary care conference"
        }
      ],
      "direct_transition": "Treatment_Selection"
    },
    "Treatment_Selection": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "NCCN risk-group-directed initial management. The 21-day deliberation",
        "period that used to sit here is now Treatment_Planning_Delay, before the",
        "conference opens, so the conference encounter closes the same day."
      ],
      "complex_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "prostate_cancer_risk",
            "operator": "==",
            "value": "low_risk"
          },
          "distributions": [
            {
              "transition": "Active_Surveillance",
              "distribution": 0.9
            },
            {
              "transition": "End_Visit_For_Surgery",
