    "Castration_Resistance_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "9%/yr progression to castration-resistant disease on androgen deprivation,",
        "plus a 2%/yr exit for durable responders discharged to routine follow-up.",
        "",
        "This arm is a blend of two populations with very different hazards: ~30%",
        "of the men here started ADT for metastatic disease at diagnosis, where",
        "the median time to castration resistance is 11-18 months (SWOG 9346;",
        "CHAARTED-era hormone-sensitive series), and ~70% started it for M0",
        "biochemical recurrence, where 10-20% progress within five years (Kirby,",
        "Int J Clin Pract 2011). The blended 9%/yr, against a 2%/yr non-CRPC",
        "discharge and competing mortality, sends roughly 60% of this arm on to",
        "castration-resistant disease over its lifetime.",
        "",
        "Competing non-prostate mortality is left to the lifecycle module, which",
        "stops this module when the person dies. The pre-2026-08 module used 60%",
        "per pass with no non-CRPC exit, so every recurrence became CRPC."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.09,
          "transition": "Metastatic_Castration_Resistant"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.02,
          "transition": "End_ADT_Stable_Discharge"
